{
  "evidence": "TEXT_G: Leave the EU to restore sovereignty and reassert supremacy of UK law; uphold Parliament, monarchy, common law, and an independent House of Lords; immigration policy aiming for near‑zero net migration with Britishness tests and tighter controls; deploy forces only in the national interest and buy British where possible; simplify benefits to encourage work/saving, stronger sentencing and more prison capacity; promote responsibility, family, and smaller government. TEXT_C: Progressive taxation up to 60%, Citizen’s Income and expanded welfare/health services; disestablish the Church of England and remove the monarchy’s formal roles; PR for Westminster and elected Lords; withdraw from Iraq, cut defence to EU average, decommission nuclear weapons; strong asylum protections and expanded migrant rights; sweeping environmental/animal-welfare measures and bans (GM, incineration, vivisection).",
  "reasoning": "The electorate weights authority and care most, with notable loyalty and proportionality; TEXT_G emphasizes restoring national sovereignty and traditional institutions (authority), protecting the ingroup via strict immigration and national‑interest defence (loyalty/ingroup‑care), and work‑encouraging welfare plus credible punishment (proportionality), while offering inward‑facing care (NHS/local safety). TEXT_C concentrates on equality and environmental purity, and explicitly dismantles traditional authorities (monarchy, established church) and advances cosmopolitan policies, aligning with lower‑weighted equality/sanctity and the subversion side of authority, making it less congruent with the profile.",
  "confidence": "high",
  "winner": "TEXT_G"
}
